12&amp;pages=726-736&amp;pmid=22342103&amp;doi=10.1016/j.ctrv.2012.01.004&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B5-cancers-15-00527"><label>5.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type="citation-string">Hoffman R.M. Development of recombinant methioninase to target the general cancer-specific metabolic defect of methionine dependence: A 40-year odyssey. Expert Opin. Biol. Ther. 2015;15:21. doi: 10.1517/14712598.2015.963050.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1517/14712598.2015.963050"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="25439528"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Expert Opin. Biol. Ther.&amp;title=Development of recombinant methioninase to target the general cancer-specific metabolic defect of methionine dependence: A 40-year odyssey&amp;author=R.M. Hoffman&amp;volume=15&amp;publication_year=2015&amp;pages=21&amp;pmid=25439528&amp;doi=10.1517/14712598.2015.963050&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B6-cancers-15-00527"><label>6.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type="citation-string">Raboni S., Montalbano S., Stransky S., Garcia B.A., Buschini A., Bettati S., Sidoli S., Mozzarelli A. A Key Silencing Histone Mark on Chromatin Is Lost When Colorectal Adenocarcinoma Cells Are Depleted of Methionine by Methionine γ-Lyase. Front. Mol. Biosci. 2021;8:735303. doi: 10.3389/fmolb.2021.735303.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.3389/fmolb.2021.735303"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmcid" xlink:href="PMC8517235"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="34660696"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Front. Mol. Biosci.&amp;title=A Key Silencing Histone Mark on Chromatin Is Lost When Colorectal Adenocarcinoma Cells Are Depleted of Methionine by Methionine γ-Lyase&amp;author=S. Raboni&amp;author=S. Montalbano&amp;author=S. Stransky&amp;author=B.A. Garcia&amp;author=A. Buschini&amp;volume=8&amp;publication_year=2021&amp;pages=735303&amp;pmid=34660696&amp;doi=10.3389/fmolb.2021.735303&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7-cancers-15-00527"><label>7.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type="citation-string">Aminabad N.S., Farshbaf M., Akbarzadeh A. Recent Advances of Gold Nanoparticles in Biomedical Applications: State of the Art. Cell Biochem. Biophys. 2019;77:123–137. doi: 10.1007/s12013-018-0863-4.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1007/s12013-018-0863-4"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="30570696"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Cell Biochem. Biophys.&amp;title=Recent Advances of Gold Nanoparticles in Biomedical Applications: State of the Art&amp;author=N.S. Aminabad&amp;author=M. Farshbaf&amp;author=A. Akbarzadeh&amp;volume=77&amp;publication_year=2019&amp;pages=123-137&amp;pmid=30570696&amp;doi=10.1007/s12013-018-0863-4&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8-cancers-15-00527"><label>8.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type="citation-string">Kawaguchi K., Han Q., Li S., Tan Y., Igarashi K., Murakami T., Unno M., Hoffman R.M. Efficacy of Recombinant Methioninase (rMETase) on Recalcitrant Cancer Patient-Derived Orthotopic Xenograft (PDOX) Mouse Models: A Review. Cells. 2019;8:410.  doi: 10.3390/cells8050410.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.3390/cells8050410"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmcid" xlink:href="PMC6562625"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="31052611"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Cells&amp;title=Efficacy of Recombinant Methioninase (rMETase) on Recalcitrant Cancer Patient-Derived Orthotopic Xenograft (PDOX) Mouse Models: A Review&amp;author=K. Kawaguchi&amp;author=Q. Han&amp;author=S. Li&amp;author=Y. Tan&amp;author=K. Igarashi&amp;volume=8&amp;publication_year=2019&amp;pages=410&amp;pmid=31052611&amp;doi=10.3390/cells8050410&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9-cancers-15-00527"><label>9.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type="citation-string">Tan Y., Xu M., Tan X., Wang X., Saikawa Y., Nagahama T., Sun X., Lenz M., Hoffman R.M. Overexpression and large-scale production of recombinant L-methionine-alpha-deamino-gammamercaptomethane- lyase for novel anticancer therapy. Protein Expr. Purif. 1997;9:233–245. doi: 10.1006/prep.1996.0700.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1006/prep.1996.0700"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="9056489"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Protein Expr. Purif.&amp;title=Overexpression and large-scale production of recombinant L-methionine-alpha-deamino-gammamercaptomethane- lyase for novel anticancer therapy&amp;author=Y. Tan&amp;author=M. Xu&amp;author=X. Tan&amp;author=X. Wang&amp;author=Y. Saikawa&amp;volume=9&amp;publication_year=1997&amp;pages=233-245&amp;pmid=9056489&amp;doi=10.1006/prep.1996.0700&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10-cancers-15-00527"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type="citation-string">Raboni S., Revtovich S., Demitri N., Giabbai B., Storici P., Cocconcelli C., Faggiano S., Rosini E., Pollegioni L., Galati S., et al.  Engineering methionine γ-lyase from Citrobacter freundii for anticancer activity. Biochim. Biophys. Acta